  - User sum `type Name = A(Int) | B(Int)` is a tagged struct. Match arms bind the Int payload. String payload `A(String)` binds `.s0`. Unit variants (`Empty`, `On`/`Off`) are bare idents, not Int payloads. Locks: `sum_shape_smoke.oo`, `sum_string_smoke.oo`, `sum_unit_smoke.oo`. Check refuses a missing user-sum arm on an annotated let (`Flag needs Off`, `Color needs Yellow`, `Either needs B`). Locks: `fixtures/sum_miss_arm.oo`, `fixtures/sum_miss_mid.oo`, `fixtures/sum_payload_miss.oo`, `fixtures/sum_all_arms.oo`, `scripts/sum_exhaust_smoke.oo`. Check binds those constructors as names (`tc_names_sum.oo`). A ctor after `=>` is not an arm (lock: `fixtures/sum_rhs_off.oo`). User-sum `_` covers leftover variants; Option/Result with only `_` still refuses.
