### Capability Model & Sandboxing
  - Process-local tokens. Landlock is a real Linux jail under `&SysCap` (`oo_landlock_restrict`). Empty allowlists fail closed. Proved `OK: LANDLOCK_JAIL` on this host.
  - POSIX `setrlimit` is product under `&SysCap` (AS / NOFILE / CPU). Zero quotas fail closed.
  - `spawn` / `wait` / `kill` are real. Child env is filtered (`OODA_`/`OO_` and `PATH`).
  - Hostile probes: `env_get` denies host keys; zero `FsWriteCap` exits; child drops `HOST_SECRET`; attenuate forged parent differs. Lock: `scripts/hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo`.
  - `process_exec` is a shell line and a secret sink.
  - `GpuCap` CPU/noop launch is product. `emit_ptx` writes real kernel PTX text (`add.s64`); device GPU dispatch is residual. Not CUDA, not a device launch.
  - Hierarchical HMAC attenuation, kernel object-cap seals, and measured isolate (hash of payload+token+domain) are product. Not SGX/TDX/SEV hardware enclaves. HMAC-SHA256 of a cap payload string is product.
  - Bump arenas (`arena_create`/`alloc`/`reset`) under AllocCap, `&ArenaCap` as its own token, and `actor_restart` under ThreadCap are product.

### Standard Library & Developer Tooling
  - Product libraries live in `ooda/std` (next to the compiler). Sibling `std/` clone is gone. GitHub `openOODA/std` is archived. Named emit+gcc+run still required.
  - vscode launches `ooda lsp`. `vscode/server/ooda-lsp.js` remains on disk and is residual. `ooda lsp` is a multi-message stdio loop. Hover and definition name the identifier under the cursor, not the first `fn`. Initialize advertises `completionProvider` (trigger `&`). `&Fs` returns `&FsCap`. Lock: `scripts/lsp_complete_smoke.oo`.
  - `ooda launch --exec NAME` runs the gated payload (not `test -e`). Path-only launch does not run. Lock: `scripts/pm_launch_exec_smoke.oo`.
  - `ooda bench FILE` times `oodac check` with `now_ms`. Prints `ooda bench: check FILE Nms`. Missing file exits 2. Lock: `scripts/bench_smoke.oo`.
  - `ooda add hello` uses the stock store (https://registry.openooda.org). `ooda search` walks every listed store. `ooda registry add https://host` adds an extra store after minisign of that host's `registry.pub`. Stock cannot be removed. Lock: `scripts/pm_store_search_smoke.oo`.
  - `ooda check`, `build`, `run`, `test`, `dump`, `outline`, `reflect`, `fix`, `patch`, `lsp`, `context`, `digest`, `health`, `pkg`, and `add` are native `.oo` in `cli/main.oo`. There is no `scripts/ooda_product.sh`.
  - Ingest git allow-list refuses HTTP, git://, and userinfo lookalikes before clone. Lock: `cli/pm_extract_proof.oo` and `qa/pm_allow_spine.oo`.
  - `crypto_sha256_internal("hello")` matches the FIPS hex. HMAC-SHA256 length is 64. AES-128-ECB encrypts one block to hex (NIST C.1).
  - Extra `oodac emit-wasm` writes a `\0asm` module and an `ooda-fns` custom section. Product `oodac/oodac` `println("Hello, openOODA!")` in `main` is WASI `fd_write` (lock: `scripts/wasm_print_lit_smoke.oo`). `fixtures/hello.oo` greet fold is WASI `fd_write` of `Hello, openOODA Developer!` (lock: `scripts/wasm_hello_smoke.oo`). Same-fn `println(ident)` of a string let is `scripts/wasm_ident_lit_smoke.oo`. Two-or-more STRING `println` join is `scripts/wasm_strcat_n_smoke.oo` and `scripts/wasm_strcat_hostile_smoke.oo`. Mixed ident+STRING stays dummy (`scripts/wasm_strcat_mixed_smoke.oo`). Two `println(STRING)` is `scripts/wasm_two_println_smoke.oo`. Mixed second print stays dummy (`scripts/wasm_two_println_hostile_smoke.oo`). `println(INT)` is `scripts/wasm_int_lit_smoke.oo`. Const `println(INT + INT)` is `scripts/wasm_add_lit_smoke.oo`. IDENT add stays dummy (`scripts/wasm_add_hostile_smoke.oo`). Const `if true` print is `scripts/wasm_if_true_smoke.oo`. Const `if false` print is `scripts/wasm_if_false_smoke.oo`. IDENT if stays dummy (`scripts/wasm_if_hostile_smoke.oo`). Three `println(STRING)` is `scripts/wasm_three_println_smoke.oo`. Const if-true no-else is `scripts/wasm_if_noelse_smoke.oo`. Const `if INT == INT` is `scripts/wasm_if_eq_smoke.oo`. IDENT third print, extra stmt beside no-else, and `if 1 == x` stay dummy. Extra println beside greet is not greet-only (`scripts/wasm_hello_hostile_smoke.oo`). Oversized print is `ERR wasm buf` (no dummy `\0asm`). Other functions keep dummy `end`. Not a browser host. Not the everyday path. `path_join` and `nfa_simulate("[ab]", …)` plus `dfa_compile` emit+gcc+run.
  - `ooda test` sets `OODA_TEST=1` and runs verify constructors plus `assert_eq!` / `assert!`. `ooda run` does not run verify blocks.
  - `ooda fix` applies `E_CAP`, `E_IMP` (missing import), `E_TC`, `E_PARSE` (missing `}`), and `E_MUST` (discarded Result → `is_err` wrap). Multi-pass, max eight. It asks yes/no before it writes, unless `--yes`. Writes go through `write_file` and need `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` (unset still denies). No TTY and no `--yes` refuses. Absolute paths and symlinks are refused. Lock: `scripts/emust_autofix_smoke.oo`.
  - `ooda patch` replaces one function body from a file (`--replace-fn` / `--with`) through `write_file`. Absolute paths, `..`, and symlinks are refused.
  - HITL is not product. The human loop is `ooda fix`.
  - Tree `oodac` emits the product CLI. `cli/host_run.oo` is 205 lines. JSON check lives in `cli/json_check.oo`.
  - Check refuses unused `Ok`/`Err`/`Some`, `let _ =` / `let _:`, discarded `expect_*`, discarded Result-returning calls such as `write_file`, and discarded user `Result` calls such as `boom();`.
