  - Extra emit-wasm writes `\0asm`. Print-lit, hello greet fold, same-fn ident-let, N-string const strcat, two-println, three-println, int-lit println, const INT+INT, if-true/if-false, if-true-no-else, if INT==INT, if INT!=INT, if-false-no-else, four-println, five-println, six-println, seven-println, const else-if, INT+INT+INT, INT-INT, INT*INT, INT/INT, INT%INT, unary-minus println, bool true/false println, if INT<INT, if INT>INT, if INT<=INT, if INT>=INT, if !true/!false, and if BOOL&&BOOL are named locks. Mixed ident concat stays dummy. Hostile second print stays dummy. IDENT if stays dummy. IDENT add stays dummy. IDENT third/fourth/fifth/sixth/seventh print, extra stmt beside no-else, if 1==x, if 1!=x, if 1<x, if 1>x, if 1<=x, if 1>=x, if !x, if true&&x, non-const else-if, IDENT in add3, IDENT sub, IDENT mul, IDENT div, IDENT mod, IDENT unary-minus, and IDENT bool stay dummy. Other fns keep dummy `end`. A browser WASM host is residual. Not a complete WASM backend.
  - Device GPU dispatch is residual. PTX text emit is product; launching on a GPU is not.
  - SGX / TDX / SEV hardware enclaves are residual. Measured isolate is product.
  - Full SMT solver / general symbolic is residual. Const + header `requires` / `ensures` / `spec` fold is product.
  - Leftover list: `ROADMAP.oot` Open. Next C work: import+call gcc, contract DOT, `Result[List[Name]]`, encoding emit-30s, named walk ERR. Stale leftover words (old cold-check seconds and module counts, import_c refuse, empty-disk registry, AES-exits, clang-link-is-next) sit in the closed stale-word log, not as this-cycle leftover. Lock: `scripts/open52_stale_smoke.oo`. Honesty rows, compiler leftovers, and library leftovers sit under Open. C emit + gcc remains the product path.

